  <link:footnoteLink xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/link" xlink:type="extended">
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-1" id="fn-1" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Property Under Capital Leases - Right of Use Operating Leases</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-2" id="fn-2" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Accumulated Provision for Depreciation includes $62,709 for accumulated amortization of Right of Use Operating Leases. See Note to Financial Statements</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-3" id="fn-3" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ASC considers the equity component of AFUDC a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes must be provided. The Respondent is required to record the deferred tax liability for AFUDC equity in Account 282 with a corresponding regulatory asset. The regulatory asset is itself a temporary difference for which deferred income taxes are recognized and recorded in Account 283. This accounting is also outlined in FERC Docket AI93-5-000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-4" id="fn-4" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As result of 2024 rate case settlement, the Partnership received FERC approval to establish $2,600,000.00 Rate Case Costs Regulatory Asset. This regulatory asset will be amortized monthly for 52 months. The initial amortization will begin on December-2024 including a catch up entry for months July-2024 through November-2024. Monthly amortization will conclude in October-2028.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-5" id="fn-5" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Northern Border "Company Use Gas Percentage" does not identify separate fuel and loss components. Therefore, gas retained from shippers is reported as "Gas Received from Shippers as Compressor Station Fuel."</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-6" id="fn-6" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other Receipts represent decreased linepack.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-7" id="fn-7" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rate schedule PAL is a balancing service, therefore, quantities are excluded as associated Dths used for balancing do not represent gas delivered.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-8" id="fn-8" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other deliveries represent increased linepack, Gas Used for Other Operations and Transmission expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Lines 9 through 29 are allocated to each rate type: Discounted Rate, Negotiated Rate and Recourse Rate, using a pro-rata allocation. The pro-rata share is determined by dividing the Shipper Supplied Gas for each rate type by the total Shipper Supplied Gas for lines 2 through 6 and multiplied by the corresponding monthly totals for lines 9 through 29.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Gas used as transmission mains gas in operations and other expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Both tracked and non-tracked fuel are valued monthly based on a 50/50 average of the Platt's Gas Daily Index for Chicago city-gates and Northern Ventura, using the index published on the last day of each month.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">General Plant includes $955,440 for Right of Use Operating Leases</link:footnote>
